# What bud mail-mcp --record does, against a server with MOVE and UIDPLUS.
# Hand-written (see login_list.imap)
S: * OK [CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 AUTH=PLAIN] IMAP4 service ready
C: a1 LOGIN "someone@example.com" "app-pass"
S: a1 OK user logged in
C: a2 CAPABILITY
S: * CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 MOVE UIDPLUS
S: a2 OK CAPABILITY completed
C: a3 LIST "" "*"
S: * LIST (\HasNoChildren \Trash) "/" "Deleted Messages"
S: * LIST (\HasNoChildren) "/" "INBOX"
S: a3 OK LIST completed
C: a4 STATUS "INBOX" (MESSAGES UNSEEN UIDNEXT UIDVALIDITY)
S: * STATUS "INBOX" (MESSAGES 3 UNSEEN 1 UIDNEXT 42 UIDVALIDITY 1700000000)
S: a4 OK STATUS completed
C: a5 EXAMINE "INBOX"
S: * 3 EXISTS
S: a5 OK [READ-ONLY] EXAMINE completed
C: a6 UID SEARCH ALL
S: * SEARCH 3 7 9
S: a6 OK SEARCH completed
C: a7 UID FETCH 7,9 (UID FLAGS RFC822.SIZE INTERNALDATE BODY.PEEK[HEADER.FIELDS (DATE FROM TO CC SUBJECT MESSAGE-ID IN-REPLY-TO REFERENCES REPLY-TO)])
S: * 2 FETCH (UID 7 FLAGS () RFC822.SIZE 100 INTERNALDATE " 3-Nov-2026 09:15:00 -0600" BODY[HEADER.FIELDS (DATE FROM TO CC SUBJECT MESSAGE-ID IN-REPLY-TO REFERENCES REPLY-TO)] {#}
L: From: Private Person <private@example.org>
L: Subject: private subject
L:
S: )
S: a7 OK FETCH completed
C: a8 UID FETCH 9 (UID RFC822.SIZE BODY.PEEK[]<0.512>)
S: * 3 FETCH (UID 9 RFC822.SIZE 100 BODY[]<0> {#}
L: Subject: secret body
L:
L: the private text
S: )
S: a8 OK FETCH completed
C: a9 LOGOUT
S: * BYE logging out
S: a9 OK LOGOUT completed
